  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#25192\", \"PowerToys#21001\", \"PowerToys#1684\"], \"answer\": \"This feature request has been filed before. PowerToys#25192 asks for a \\\"Copy as plain text\\\" option, and PowerToys#21001 asks to copy text without formatting. PowerToys#21001 was closed as a duplicate of PowerToys#1684, the original Paste as Plain Text request, which also has a suggestion for a Ctrl+Shift+C copy-as-plain-text shortcut. The archive shows no implemented copy-as-plain-text feature, so there is no built-in fix yet. You can add your use case, the LibreOffice Writer behaviour you saw, to those tickets as a thumbs-up or comment. Until then, the workaround the tickets describe is to paste into a plain editor such as Notepad or the Run prompt and copy the text again. You can also use the paste-as-plain-text function inside the destination app, as you already do.\"}",
